  "_comment": "Negative, and the one that proves the disabling actually holds. The finding never names the closure claim directly \u2014 it reaches it through rkaf:findingProofRecord and then rkaf:proofSupportingRecord. 'Disabled' has to mean UNREACHABLE rather than un-named, or omission gets enabled by indirection. Caught by rkaf:ClosureClaimNotFindingEvidenceShape (spec/rkaf-analysis.md 6). This is the ONLY class of fixture permitted to contain a ClosureClaim and a RelationFinding together, and it must fail."
